@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Demonstrates basic sequence-diagram concepts: lifelines, synchronous messages, and return arrows
'   usecase:      Educational example showing the minimum vocabulary needed to read a UML sequence diagram
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       Authentication
' ============================================================================
title Example Sequence Diagram - Simple Login Flow

' ============================================================================
' CONCEPTS TAUGHT
'   - actor            : a human participant rendered as a stick figure
'   - participant      : a software/system participant rendered as a box
'   - lifeline         : the vertical dashed line descending from each
'                        participant; time flows top -> bottom
'   - -> (sync)        : solid line, FILLED arrowhead = synchronous call,
'                        caller blocks waiting for a reply
'   - --> (return)     : DASHED line = reply / return value back to caller
' ============================================================================

' Actors are drawn as stick figures (human users).
' Participants are drawn as rectangular boxes (software components).
actor "User" as U
participant "Web App" as W
participant "Auth Service" as A

' Each message is ordered top-to-bottom; the vertical ordering IS the
' chronological order of the interaction.

' Synchronous call: caller blocks until the receiver replies.
' PlantUML syntax: Sender -> Receiver : label
U -> W : enterCredentials()
activate W
' "activate" draws an execution bar (activation box) on W's lifeline to show
' W is actively executing while waiting for the next reply.
W -> A : authenticate(email, password)
activate A

' Return / reply: dashed arrow back to the caller with the result.
A --> W : token (or error)
deactivate A

W --> U : renderDashboard()
deactivate W

@enduml
